</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>otherwise.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>is_floating_point_v</computeroutput> variable template evaluates to <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if the given type <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is a floating point type (<computeroutput>float</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>double</computeroutput>, or <computeroutput>long double</computeroutput>). For all other types, it evaluates to <computeroutput>false</computeroutput>. This trait is used throughout the µTest++ framework to enable type-safe handling and specialisation for floating point types in template metaprogramming.</para>
<para>Specialisations are provided for <computeroutput>float</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>double</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>long double</computeroutput>, each evaluating to <computeroutput>true</computeroutput>. </para>
